Now, I need to find GCD(4n + 5, 3n + 1). Let me apply the Euclidean algorithm again here. So, now I have two expressions: C = 4n + 5 and D = 3n + 1. So, similar to before, I can compute GCD(C, D) by finding C mod D or D mod C. Let me try to do that. 

